From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] fix(macos): actually suppress mapped mouse events

core-graphics 0.24 treats a None event-tap callback result as
pass-through, so mapped mouse buttons and wheel events still reach
applications after Kanata forwards them for remapping.

Upgrade to core-graphics 0.25 and use its explicit
`CallbackResult::Drop` and `CallbackResult::Keep` API. Retain the
Session tap location and pass movement events through to avoid the
Bluetooth cursor regressions in #739 and #1636.
---
